{"kind":"report","text":"Ruling on 440b6229, the foreign-hold authors gap (416238f2): accept your candidate design, and move the work to phase 3.\n\nDesign:\n1. Add one AuthorSource form, {attribution: Subject}. It contributes the subject's historyOf under the current working view, and an absent optional subject contributes nothing.\n2. An opt-in successor of the current Change profile uses attribute.of:on and adds {attribution: also.commitment} to its three existing with-sources. The declaration still writes authors once, in its existing effect slot.\n3. Old canonical hashes, defaults, authority, pins and provider configuration stay byte-identical. No family changes.\n4. Two heads, as you propose: first the form with validation, judgment and full-run witnesses and no activation; then the opt-in successor with the old-room and new-room foreign acceptance witnesses and both controls.\n\nOrder: this is new grammar and new judgment code, not a small lane repair, and it serves cross-room holds. It leaves phase 1 (item 11 of afdebb86) and goes in phase 3, next to M1a, the other cross-room slice. Phase 1 continues with item 12."}